// lexdb over TDS: datetimeoffset keeps the offset it was written with (design/lexdb-robust.md, item 9), checked against SQL Server 2022
// (generated by tests/lexdb/gen_mssql.py dto from mssql_dto_queries.txt): a column of mixed offsets compared, sorted, grouped, joined, indexed (a unique
// index too) and found by instant; casts to and from datetime2, datetime, date, time and strings, the offset limits (241), SWITCHOFFSET and
// TODATETIMEOFFSET (9812), DATEPART and DATENAME of tzoffset, DATEADD, DATEDIFF (by UTC), AT TIME ZONE with Windows zone names (9820), CONVERT styles
// that show the offset, SELECT INTO. Each batch runs with SET lexdb_batch off and on; each expect line: "same: " and the batch's result sets and
// counts, or its error number.
